The EdgeRouter X trove: three donated routers made dumb switches

troves/edgerouter-x: one config (switch.cfg) that makes any EdgeRouter X a
five-port gigabit switch with no routing, NAT, DHCP server or cloud, and the
recipe to prepare each unit from a factory reset.

- [x] unit 1 reset and read (EdgeOS v2.0.9-hotfix.2, factory config)
- [x] switch.cfg drafted: all ports in switch0, DHCP management, UNMS off
- [x] login password generated into Credential Manager (fcpm-edgerouter-x:ubnt), not in any file
- [x] Autumn approved switch.cfg; units 1, 2 and 3 prepared (both phases, confirmed by link-local)
- [x] EdgeOS v3 (unit 2) refuses a password without a symbol: shared password rotated to one with a symbol
- [ ] the three join the studio network (DHCP; reservations if fixed numbers wanted)
